\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Japan \highlight\uc2  BOJ Reform Panel -3:  \highlight22\uc2 Forex Intervention \highlight\uc2  Govt Priority \b0\par\par\uc2 269 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 September 1996\par 11:57\par \uc2  Capital Markets Report \par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1996, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    As for the second area of the Bank of Japan's primary\par business \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , Torii repeated that the primary\par responsibility of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets should\par rest with the government.\par    For \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  usually are related to\par stability in yen-dollar exchange rates which reflect\par bilateral relationships between Japan and the U.S. This\par indicates that decisions on \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  are\par highly political and are best suited for governments to\par handle, Torii said.\par    For the third area of the Bank of Japan \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ,\par Torii said the panel agreed a close consultation is\par necessary between the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and the government on\par matters related to financial system stability.\par    Such a cooperative relationship is necessary even as the\par Bank of Japan secures independence on monetary policy, Torii\par said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  The Bank of Japan's monetary policy is inseparable\par from the government's economic policy and both sides have\par kept a forum for coordination even under the current law, he\par said.\par    The panel has yet to conclude on who should ultimately\par be responsible in an unrealistic, but theoretically\par possible, case when an agreement isn't reached, he said.\par    As for the appointment of senior Bank of Japan\par officials, the panel generally agrees that the cabinet\par should have the power to appoint senior \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par officials but no conclusion has been drawn for whether to\par require parliamentary confirmation, Torii said.\par    But the government shouldn't have the right to dismiss\par policy board members, the panel said.\par    The panel will next meet on Sept. 18.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (END) DOW JONES NEWS 09-11-96\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 0557EDT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  4077 \par \par \uc2 Dokument cm00000020011013ds9b0230a\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
