\par\par \b \uc2  Tokyo Midday: Dlr Mixed; BOJ Rumors Seen Groundless \b0\par\par\uc2 320 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 August 1996\par 04:14\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1996, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TOKYO (AP-Dow Jones)--Moderate selling by institutional investors led the dollar slightly weaker against the yen at midday in Tokyo Tuesday from its levels early in the session while it remains unchanged against the Deutsche mark. \par \par \uc2  The market continues to focus on the mark rather than the dollar, a trader at a Japanese commercial bank said. Although Asian dealings will focus on mark selling for yen and to some extent the Swiss franc, global dealings are likely to see selling of the German unit across the board, particularly against other European \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , he said. \par \par \uc2  The potential sell-off of marks stems from the potential decrease in interest rate differentials between Germany and other countries, particularly Japan. \par \par \uc2  While traders see rate rises by the Bank of Japan as only a matter of time, they see the German \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  possibly cutting its securities repurchase rate soon. \par \par \uc2  A shrink in interest rate differentials between Germany and other countries is seen to lessen the attractiveness of mark-denominated assets. \par \par \uc2  Rumors that the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the dollar earlier were dismissed by market participants. \par \par \uc2  The dollar rose to its intraday high of 106.64 yen around 0019 GMT not from BOJ buying but from a large order by a U.S. investment bank, a trader at a Japanese long-term credit bank said. \par \par \uc2  Around 0200 GMT, the dollar is trading at 106.65 yen, up from 106.62 yen around 0030 GMT but below 106.68 yen in New York late Monday. The dollar was quoted at 106.90 yen in Tokyo late Monday. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is also trading at 1.4822 Deutsche marks, flat from earlier in Tokyo but below 1.4825 marks late Monday in New York. The dollar was at 1.4738 marks in Tokyo late Monday. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 05-08-96 \par \par \uc2  0214GMT \par \par \uc2  1074 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011013ds8606bpe\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
