\par\par \b \uc2  Early Tokyo: Dlr Up Slightly, But Looks Top-Heavy \b0\par\par\uc2 372 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 August 1996\par 02:34\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1996, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TOKYO (AP-Dow Jones)--The dollar is slightly higher in early Tokyo trading Monday than its levels late in New York Friday, but market participants agree the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  looks top heavy for the time being. \par \par \uc2  Friday's weaker-than-expected U.S. jobs data may have reassured the U.S. stock and bond markets, but the dollar got little benefit from the perception that U.S. interest rates are less likely to go up soon, nor is it likely to, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  'Last week confirmed the dollar's top-heaviness, and this week should see it move down slowly,' said a trader at a Japanese bank. \par \par \uc2  The one thing that could buoy the dollar is fears of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  (BOJ) to prop up the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Until Friday, when unconfirmed rumors of BOJ buying gave the dollar a brief boost, most traders had said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was unlikely to come in to support the dollar unless it threatened to go below 105.00 yen. That sentiment seems to have changed. \par \par \uc2  If the dollar moves down, 'there will be rumors of BOJ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  around 106.30 yen,' said a trader at a U.S. bank in Tokyo. 'But the market... will try the downside anyway.' \par \par \uc2  Around 0030 GMT, the dollar is trading at 106.85 yen, down from 106.88 yen around 0001 GMT but above 106.78 yen in New York late Friday. The dollar was quoted at 107.06 yen late in Tokyo Friday. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is also trading at 1.4762 Deutsche marks, higher than 1.4755 marks around 0001 GMT and just above 1.4758 marks late Friday in New York. The dollar was at 1.4788 marks in Tokyo late Friday. \par \par \uc2  The mark is trading at 72.38 yen, down from 72.44 yen around 0001 GMT but above 72.35 yen in New York late Friday. The mark was quoted late in Tokyo Friday at 72.40 yen. \par \par \uc2  The dollar is seen trading between 106.50-107.30 yen and 1.4740-1.4790 marks for the rest of the Asian day. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 04-08-96 \par \par \uc2  0034GMT \par \par \uc2  1074 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011013ds8506coj\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
