\par\par \b \uc2  Asia  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  Roundup: Dlr Mixed; BOJ Buy Rumors Questioned \b0\par\par\uc2  By John Brinsley \par \uc2 380 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 August 1996\par 07:44\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1996, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TOKYO (AP-Dow Jones)--Was there or wasn't there? \par \par \uc2  That was the question late in Tokyo trading Friday as rumors of Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  (BOJ) \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  helped send the dollar up sharply against the yen in the early afternoon, although the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is now lower than its levels Thursday in New York. \par \par \uc2  The dollar is up against the Deutsche mark, however, as mark selling for yen helped bring the Germany \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  down. \par \par \uc2  The dollar shot up to an intraday high of 107.25 yen around 0418 gmt from 106.75 around 0330 GMT when rumors the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was in the market began to circulate. The rumors took participants by surprise, as most had expected a fairly quiet session of shoring up positions ahead of the release of key economic data in the U.S. later in the day. \par \par \uc2  The news was first discounted by dealers in Tokyo then in Singapore, as rumors that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  there kept the market wondering. \par \par \uc2  With few exceptions, most traders were skeptical that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2 , with many saying the 105.00-yen level remains the place to watch for such action. \par \par \uc2  'I haven't heard anything except rumors,' said a trader at a Japanese bank. \par \par \uc2  A trader at a U.S. bank in Tokyo agreed, saying that short-covering after the dollar moved down in the morning session had helped to bring the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  back up. \par \par \uc2  'There's been real buying demand by (Japanese) life insurers,' he added. \par \par \uc2  But some were less quick to dismiss the speculation. \par \par \uc2  'My feeling is that the Japanese financial authorities would like to protect the 106-yen level, because if they don't, the dollar will fall below 105 yen, maybe to 103 yen,' said a dealer at a European bank in Tokyo. \par \par \uc2  Around 0530 GMT, the dollar is quoted at 107.06 yen, just below 107.10 yen late Thursday in New York but up from 106.77 yen late Thursday in London. \par \par \uc2  The dollar also is at 1.4788 marks, higher than 1.4761 marks late Thursday in New York and above 1.4739 marks in London Thursday. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 02-08-96 \par \par \uc2  0544GMT \par \par \uc2  1034 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011013ds8206ed5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
