\par\par \b \uc2  Asia  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  Roundup:Dlr Rebounds After MOF Official Remarks \b0\par\par\uc2  By Brian Fowler \par \uc2 282 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 August 1996\par 07:37\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1996, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TOKYO (AP-Dow Jones)--The dollar rebounded Thursday after comments made by a Japan \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  official, and remains higher in Tokyo trading late Thursday compared with levels in New York late Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Traders said the dollar's plunge against the yen overnight left the market wary of possible Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  (BOJ) \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The official's comments, with those concerns as a backdrop, sparked a wave of short-covering dollar buying, said Yasuhisa Morikuni, customer dealer at Bank of America in Tokyo. \par \par \uc2  As reported, the official, who declined to be named, told AP-Dow Jones that the dollar's plunge against the yen overnight 'didn't reflect fundamentals and was only temporary.' \par \par \uc2  Morikuni said the market interpreted the official's comments as a message from the BOJ. \par \par \uc2  Satoshi Inoue, manager of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  at Bank of Tokyo Mitsubishi, added, 'The market was short (on dollars) at the moment that the comments appeared, so they supported the dollar.' \par \par \uc2  Around 0520 GMT, the dollar is quoted at 107.35 yen, above 106.83 yen late Wednesday in New York and well up from 106.76 yen late Wednesday in London. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  also is at 1.4743 Deutsche marks, higher than 1.4725 marks late Wednesday in New York and above 1.4722 marks in London Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  The mark is quoted at 72.81 yen, up from 72.55 yen in New York late Wednesday and above 72.52 yen in London late Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Sterling is at $1.5563, up from $1.5561 in New York late Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 01-08-96 \par \par \uc2  0537GMT \par \par \uc2  1034 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011013ds81069ah\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
