\par\par \b \uc2  BOJ's July dollar purchases estimated at $567 mln. \b0\par\par\uc2 235 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 August 1996\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1996 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, Aug 1 (Reuter) - The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  (BOJ) bought an estimated $567 million in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in July, up from $196 million in June, bankers said on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  The figures include the last two trading days of June but not the last two business days of July, as \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  settlements are made two days after the transactions. \par \par \uc2  BOJ data, released on Thursday, showed that capital outlays from the government's special \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  account to the private sector totalled 61 billion yen in July. \par \par \uc2  The figure consists mostly of yen payments from the government \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  account to the private sector, mainly commercial banks. Those yen payments are a result of dollar-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the yen by the BOJ. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which manages the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  account, raises yen cash for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by issuing special financing bills (FBs) for \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The FBs are also used for converting dollar-denominated gains on the government external reserves into yen. \par \par \uc2  Outstanding FBs as of July 31 totalled 28.927 trillion yen, up by 78 billion yen from a month earlier. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar rose to 111.20 yen on July 8 in Tokyo, its highest level since January, 1994. On July 31 in New York, it fell to 106.35 yen. -- Tokyo Treasury Desk (813-3432-8676) \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1996 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011018ds8104vwi\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
