\par\par \b \uc2  BOJ says no comment on  \highlight22\uc2 forex intervention \highlight\uc2  report. \b0\par\par\uc2 251 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 Juli 1996\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1996 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, July 29 (Reuter) - The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Monday it would not comment on a weekend newspaper report that the BOJ and Japanese business leaders believe the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  should be given more authority and responsibility to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. \par \par \uc2  The financial daily Nihon Keizai Shimbun said on Saturday this could be a possible topic of discussion at a meeting which begins on Wednesday on the revision of the BOJ law by a special research group formed by Prime Minister Ryutaro Hashimoto. \par \par \uc2  The paper said the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which currently decides on \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , opposes the idea. \par \par \uc2  BOJ officials told Reuters that there were currently no discussions on the matter, and they were not sure whether the subject would come up at the meeting. \par \par \uc2  Under current rules, the BOJ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market only on the express instructions of the Finance Ministry, the daily said. It said such voices expressing the need to boost the BOJ's authority to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  were also heard within the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Business leaders also saw the need to reform rules that could make the BOJ more independent. \par \par \uc2  An official at the Japan Association of Corporate Executives quoted chairman Jiro Ushio as saying that the BOJ's administrative power is generally weak compared with global standards. \par \par \uc2  The newspaper quoted BOJ sources as saying that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has less influence in deciding on \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  compared with other industrialised nations. \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1996 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011018ds7t04zci\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
