\par\par \b \uc2  Japan Debt Narrowly Mixed; Supported By BOJ Bond Purchase \b0\par\par\uc2 290 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Juni 1996\par 04:50\par \uc2  Capital Markets Report \par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1996, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    TOKYO (Dow Jones)--Prices of Japanese debt securities\par are narrowly mixed Wednesday morning.\par    Prices dropped at the open on profit-taking and the\par dollar's appreciation, but later rebounded. Traders say\par the Bank of Japan's outright purchase of government bonds\par supported the market.\par    The Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  didn't \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the money\par market, in line with expectations, to leave bank reserves\par comfortably above the requirement. The key unsecured rate\par for overnight call money was unchanged at 0.49%.\par    TIFFE Dec 3-Mos Euroyen Yield:     1.03%   Up 0.01\par    TSE Sept 5-Yr JGB Future Price:    112.21  Up 0.02\par    TSE Sept 10-Yr JGB Future Price:   118.92  Dn 0.03\par    10-Yr 3.0% JGB No. 182 Yield:      3.155%  Up 0.01\par    The price of the benchmark 10-year bond, the Finance\par Ministry's No. 182, 3.0% coupon due in 2005, ended the\par Tokyo Stock Exchange's (TSE) morning session at 98.88,\par down 0.07 from the Tuesday close.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    "The market found some profit-takers at the top of its\par recent trading range, but downward pressure was limited,"\par says a trader at a large Japanese securities company.\par "The Bank of Japan's outright bond purchase was in line\par with expectations, and helped prices to regain."\par    The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said it was looking to buy 200\par billion yen of bonds outright, the first such purchase\par for this month. (See CMR page [4038].)\par    Traders say although market participants will closely\par monitor fluctuations in the dollar-yen exchange rate, the\par current trading level in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market\par hasn't much affected the debt market.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (MORE) DOW JONES NEWS 06-04-96\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 2250EDT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  4077 4118 4153 \par \par \uc2 Dokument cm00000020011013ds6501b2r\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
