\par\par \b \uc2  =Intl Monetary Conference Roundup: Greenspan Bullish On U.S. \b0\par\par\uc2 325 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 Juni 1996\par 11:37\par \uc2  Capital Markets Report \par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1996, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  == Chairman of the U.S. Federal Reserve Board Alan Greenspan was reportedly bullish on the U.S. economy when briefing top-level commercial bankers at the International Monetary Conference Sunday [4201]. \par \par \uc2  == Chairman of the U.S. Federal Reserve Alan Greenspan reportedly said Sunday that the U.S. economy has come through its inventory adjustment smoothly and that he thinks asset prices are in check [4210]. \par \par \uc2  == Prices of U.S. Treasurys in Tokyo were lower Monday afternoon, following comments by Federal Reserve Chairman Greenspan who noted that his comments contained both bullish and bearish factors [4041]. \par \par \uc2  == The Governor of the Bank of England Eddie George said the U.K. is experiencing a "relatively stable situation" with monetary policy at present, but he sees a risk of inflation rekindling in 1998 [4204]. \par \par \uc2  == Bank of France Governor Jean-Claude Trichet termed domestic economic indicators "encouraging" and said that, in some respects, it appears the French economy is on its "starting blocks," at the IMC conference Sunday [4206]. \par \par \uc2  == The Bank of Japan's monetary policy continues to aim at ensuring current recovery on self-sustainable growth led by private demand, and while Japan's economy has resumed growth late last year and is gradually recovering, the BOJ still sees downside risk from ongoing structural adjustments, said Akira Nagashima, deputy governor for international relations, speaking at the IMC [4203]. \par \par \uc2  == Akira Nagashima, a deputy governor of the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 , said the G-7 will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets if movements in these markets aren't justified by economic fundamentals, at a press briefing at the annual International Monetary Conference [4202]. \par \par \uc2  == Reserve Bank of Australia Governor Bernie Fraser said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  isn't contemplating any immediate change in monetary policy, speaking at a briefing for journalists after a meeting of central bankers at the International Monetary Conference [4205]. \par \par \uc2  (END) DOW JONES NEWS 06-03-96 \par \par \uc2  0537EDT \par \par \uc2  4012 4035 4077 4128 \par \par \uc2 Dokument cm00000020011013ds6301ad0\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
