\par\par \b \uc2  Asia  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  Roundup -2: Market Looks To Friday's PPI Data \b0\par\par\uc2 329 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 Mai 1996\par 08:44\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1996, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  The Australian dollar was trading at $0.8000, down from $0.8012 Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Traders said the market is looking ahead to the release Friday of U.S. Producer Price Index (PPI) data for April. If the numbers indicate an inflationary trend, they could spark fears of interest rate hikes. \par \par \uc2  Normally, that might give the dollar a boost, but the U.S. stock and bonds markets have fallen on strong economic data recently, harming the dollar as well. \par \par \uc2  'People want to have some hint whether U.S. inflation is really going on,' said Nao Nakajima, a vice president at Bank of America in Tokyo. 'I think the PPI numbers will be important. Right now there's no other real news.' \par \par \uc2  April's PPI is seen up 0.5%, and excluding volatile food and energy prices should rise 0.2%, according to a survey of economists by AP-Dow Jones. \par \par \uc2  If the numbers show signs of inflation, the dollar could fall sharply, traders said, as support for the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  seems tentative. \par \par \uc2  'Right now there's no real reason to buy the dollar,' said a dealer at a Japanese commercial bank. He said the dollar could fall as far as 103.00 yen and 1.5100 marks before finding support. \par \par \uc2  While two weeks ago the market seemed convinced the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  (BOJ) would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to protect the dollar around the 105.00-yen level, sentiment has changed, traders said. \par \par \uc2  'The BOJ didn't come in last week when the dollar went down to 103.80 yen,' said the Japanese bank dealer. He said the fact that the dollar found support at that level may have convinced the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stay out. \par \par \uc2  But others aren't so sure. Traders said memories of BOJ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in February could keep the dollar from moving to the 103.00-yen level. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 09-05-96 \par \par \uc2  0644GMT \par \par \uc2  1034 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011013ds5903vyq\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
