\par\par \b \uc2  BOJ -  \highlight22\uc2 Intervene \highlight\uc2  -2-:  \highlight22\uc2 Japan \highlight\uc2  Stk Mkt Discounts Stronger Yen \b0\par\par\uc2 435 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 April 1996\par 14:09\par \uc2  Dow Jones News Service \par \uc2 DJ\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1996, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  Banque Paribas' Parsons, who feels this will be the most crucial week of the year for dollar/yen rates, warned against underestimating the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's skill at \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  ''In February, it showed it was acutely aware of chart levels and attuned to market psychology,'' he said, suggesting that the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may be waiting to create ''an elaborate bear-trap.'' \par \par \uc2  But some fear disaster could strike if the dollar drops below a key chart level at 103.80 yen. Then, as more players move to cover short positions, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  might find itself having to fight a much bigger battle than it potentially has on its hands now. \par \par \uc2  ''The time is past for subtlety,'' Parsons said, suggesting that the Bank of Japan might then have to turn to its partners in the Group of Seven major industrialized countries to launch a more substantial coordinated exercise to save the dollar. \par \par \uc2  Although NatWest's Ferridge doesn't share Parsons' fears of a dramatic dollar rout, he does see the Bank of Japan coming under pressure to give the dollar a nudge sooner rather than later. \par \par \uc2  Apart from U.S. and German concerns, Japan's own equity market has started to discount the costs of a stronger yen with the Nikkei losing 193.73 points to close at 22041.30 this session. \par \par \uc2  Early today in Europe, the dollar was down at 104.25 yen from 104.75 yen. At one stage, it had fallen as far as 104.02 yen. \par \par \uc2  The dollar is also now down at 1.5264 Deutsche marks from 1.5268 marks after falling as low as 1.5220 marks. \par \par \uc2  Analysts noted that the mark continued to come under heavy pressure against the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  as well, falling to 68.32 yen from 68.61 yen. Although there are regular support intervals on the way down, no solid floor is expected to emerge until it gets down as far as 65.00 yen. \par \par \uc2  The slide has helped renew mark weakness against its European counterparts, a shift that many expect the German authorities to take exception to given continued signs that the German economy remains deeply depressed. \par \par \uc2  However, with U.S. bond markets growing edgy about the release of the latest batch of U.S. employment data Friday, some see the mark at least making gains against the dollar, as investors step back from U.S. asset markets. \par \par \uc2  ''I don't think the dollar/mark can shrug this all off entirely,'' Parsons said. \par \par \uc2  (END) DOW JONES NEWS 04-30-96 \par \par \uc2  8:09 AM \par \par \uc2 Dokument dj00000020011013ds4u02i7z\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw427\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal6405\pichgoal600
