\par\par \b \uc2  BOJ May Be Pressured To  \highlight22\uc2 Intervene \highlight\uc2  To Boost Dollar \b0\par\par\uc2  By Nicholas Hastings \par \uc2 381 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 April 1996\par 13:59\par \uc2  Dow Jones News Service \par \uc2 DJ\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1996, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  LONDON (Dow Jones)--The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been playing a subtle game of hide-and-seek with the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market but it may come under pressure from both the U.S. and Germany to start defending the dollar soon. \par \par \uc2  ''This is not going to please the Germans,'' Lee Ferridge, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  analyst at NatWest Markets, commented as the yen's continued rise helped to put the Deutsche mark under pressure against its European counterparts. \par \par \uc2  Nick Parsons, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Banque Paribas, is already bracing himself for Germany to try talking the dollar up again. \par \par \uc2  ''This means the (Deutsche) Bundesbank is unlikely to remain silent,'' he said, noting that German policy has almost entirely shifted toward ensuring some stimulus for its ailing economy. \par \par \uc2  He noted that the U.S. has already waded in with the Deputy U.S. Treasury Secretary Lawrence Summers pointing out late yesterday that ''a strong dollar is very much in America's interests.'' \par \par \uc2  Although analysts doubt that there is any need for coordinated market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to boost the dollar at this stage, some are worried that the Bank of Japan may have underestimated the sheer size of the short yen positions to be covered and are running the risk of another speculative bubble on the downside. \par \par \uc2  ''The danger at the moment is that the (Bank of Japan's) signals are too subtle,'' Parsons said. ''What they may need to do is wheel out the blunt instruments.'' \par \par \uc2  Market sensitivity to the Bank of Japan's intentions has become particularly acute as the dollar drifted back to nearly 104.00 yen - a level that triggered a massive \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  exercise two months ago. \par \par \uc2  Although an apparent shift in the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's monetary policy since then has probably reduced its enthusiasm for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , many feel market conditions this week are probably ideal for early action. \par \par \uc2  ''If it doesn't take advantage of the illiquid markets to squeeze out the shorts this week, I doubt they will come in next week under normal conditions,'' Parsons said, referring to the so-called Golden Week of holidays that closed Japanese markets on yesterday and will close them again Friday and coming Monday. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) DOW JONES NEWS 04-30-96 \par \par \uc2  7:59 AM \par \par \uc2 Dokument dj00000020011013ds4u02i5m\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
