\par\par \b \uc2  Dollar eases back vs yen, mark/yen falls in Tokyo. \b0\par\par\uc2 311 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 April 1996\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1996 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, April 26 (Reuter) - ASIAN \b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  ACTIVITY; \par \par \uc2  *Dollar eased back against yen on position adjustment by interbank traders ahead of long weekend in Japan and persistent selling pressure from U.S. hedge funds and others above 106.80 yen, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  *Dollar sales prompted by perceptions that dollar recovery had reached limits by midday. "Selling pressure from U.S. funds is persistent and heavy, they have been selling dollars for yen all the way from 109 yen," said a dealer. \par \par \uc2  *Mark slipped against yen, but sporadic mark short-cover buying could emerge between 69.50 and 69.00 yen, he added. \par \par \uc2  0300 GMT \par \par \uc2  *Dollar rebounded strongly from earlier dive against yen and stood slightly higher than New York close at Tokyo noon. \par \par \uc2  *Apparent dollar buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  (BOJ), combined with short-covering of marks for yen lifted dollar off lows set earlier on renewed concerns over expectations of higher Japanese interest rates, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  *After dipping as low as 106.10 yen on newspaper report saying BOJ has begun to consider altering current accommodative credit policy, dollar posted an impressive recovery on waves of buying triggered by the apparent BOJ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  *BOJ seen buying dollars at around 106.20-30 yen. \par \par \uc2  *Dealers also said there was talk the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore (MAS) buying dollars on behalf of the BOJ. \par \par \uc2  *They said Singapore-based Swiss banks were particularly active dollar buyers for yen, leading to speculation of MAS \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  at request of Japanese authorities. \par \par \uc2  *Dealers also said commercial dollar purchases at 0100 GMT local fixing and some buying on dips at around 106.30 yen by Japanese investors limited dollar's initial fall. \par \par \uc2  *But dollar's topside remains heavily capped at 107.00 yen, with light exporter sales already detected at 106.80 yen. \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1996 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011018ds4q08pyq\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
