\par\par \b \uc2  BOJ dlr-buying may not boost money supply - governor. \b0\par\par\uc2 356 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 April 1996\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1996 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, April 16 (Reuter) - Japan's money supply is unlikely to be boosted because of any dollar-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  (BOJ) in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets, BOJ Governor Yasuo Matsushita told a key parliamentary panel on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Japan's money supply is now growing gradually in a stable manner, he added. \par \par \uc2  If the BOJ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets to buy dollars for yen, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  also conducts necessary market \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prevent any excessive surplus or shortage of funds in the money market, Matsushita told the Upper House of parliament's budget committee. \par \par \uc2  "It is unlikely that our dollar buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  will immediately prompt declines in market interest rates or activate bank lending to increase the nation's money supply," Matsushita said, when asked about the possible impact of BOJ dollar-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the nation's money supply growth. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's money supply growth is not the sole target of the BOJ's monetary policy, but the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  believes money supply is one of the very important items of economic data indicating possible changes in the overall economy, he said. \par \par \uc2  "At present, money supply growth has stabilised well and is now moving gradually," he added. \par \par \uc2  The governor also said the BOJ has started to employ two key measures in managing its monetary policy since last year, namely a change in the discount rate and market \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 . He said the BOJ hopes to improve the management of monetary policy in the future. He but did not elaborate. \par \par \uc2  Eisuke Sakakibara, director-general of the Finance Ministry's International Finance Bureau, told the same committee on Tuesday that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's monetary authorities have \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets only in cases where \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  deviated from economic fundamentals. \par \par \uc2  "The yen's rally last year deviated greatly from economic fundamentals," Sakakibara said. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's dollar-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets at that time was within the framework of policy coordination between the Group of Seven nations, which agreed last April to seek an orderly reversal of the yen's strength, he said. \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1996 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011018ds4g0999y\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
