\par\par \b \uc2  World  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  -3: Traders Bullish Despite Dollar Lethargy \b0\par\par\uc2 298 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 1996\par 23:13\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1996, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  Upward dollar moves versus the yen were also interrupted by exporters ready to sell the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  starting at 106.40 yen, according to Andrew Harris, a \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer at Nippon Credit Bank in New York. \par \par \uc2  On the flip side of the coin, however, traders said strengthening of the yen is limited by concerns over tensions between China and Taiwan. \par \par \uc2  A second round of Chinese military exercises began Tuesday with maneuvers by ships and planes near Taiwanese islets. Chinese officials have confirmed the war games are intended to intimidate Taiwan ahead of its March 23 presidential elections. \par \par \uc2  Merrill's Grigull also said rising global oil prices may be lending to negative yen sentiment. 'There's pressure on oil prices and Japan is a big importer of oil,' he said. However, he noted the correlation between oil prices and the dollar-yen rate isn't consistent. \par \par \uc2  Both Grigull and Harris said they remain bullish on the dollar, despite its current lethargy. \par \par \uc2  Harris said he gives the dollar a 70% chance of hitting 107 yen before the end of March. And come April, when Japan begins a new fiscal year, he said he thinks the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  'might come in stronger,' \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets to promote a weaker yen versus the dollar. \par \par \uc2  In other trading, the Swedish krona gained against the mark and dollar, partly in response to a cut in the country's securities repurchase, or repo, rate. \par \par \uc2  Sweden's Riksbank cut 0.25 percentage point off its repo rate to 7.60%, its sixth cut in the key rate so far this year. \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  officials said the rate cut was justified by lower inflation. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 19-03-96 \par \par \uc2  2213GMT \par \par \uc2  1033 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011013ds3j02hiy\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
