\par\par \b \uc2  Surprise  \highlight22\uc2 forex \highlight\uc2  announcement unlikely at APEC - MOF. \b0\par\par\uc2 204 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 1996\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1996 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  KYOTO, Japan, March 16 (Reuter) - Finance ministers from the Asia-Pacific Economic Cooperation (APEC) economies are unlikely to make a surprise announcement on \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Sunday, when they end a two-day meeting in Kyoto, a senior Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  official told Reuters on Saturday. \par \par \uc2  Asked whether the APEC ministers will make any surprise announcement to ensure stability in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets, the official said: "I'm afraid there is a misunderstanding... No surprise announcements are likely to come out tomorrow." \par \par \uc2  He said that in earlier bilateral meetings between Japanese Finance Minister Wataru Kubo and other APEC ministers, there was no discussion of a fresh initiative on \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , such as the expansion of an Asian repurchase agreement or \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by other nations on behalf of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  He said such issues were unlikely to be discussed at the official APEC finance ministers' meetings on Sunday. \par \par \uc2  Asked about Saturday's meeting between Kubo and U.S. Treasury Secretary Robert Rubin, in which the ministers agreed to continue to cooperate closely in \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in line with previous commitments, the official said the agreement showed that there had been no change in both countries' stance towards \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1996 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011019ds3g00ant\par }\page {\