\par\par \b \uc2  Tokyo Midday: Dlr Marginally Higher; Range Seen Narrow \b0\par\par\uc2 311 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 1996\par 03:20\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1996, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TOKYO (AP-Dow Jones)--The dollar is marginally higher midday in Tokyo Thursday from its earlier levels, as some selling interest from Japanese exporters is countered by wariness of Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , traders said. \par \par \uc2  'It's a typical sandwich market,' said a trader at a European bank in Tokyo. \par \par \uc2  Around 0215 GMT, the dollar is trading at 105.25 yen, slightly higher than 105.23 yen around 0030 GMT and above 105.15 yen in New York late Wednesday. The dollar was quoted at 105.30 yen in Tokyo late Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is also trading at 1.4730 Deutsche marks, barely above 1.4728 marks earlier in Tokyo and up from 1.4708 marks late Wednesday in New York. The dollar was at 1.4750 marks in Tokyo late Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  The mark is at 71.47 yen, up from 71.45 yen earlier in Tokyo but below 71.49 yen in New York late Wednesday. The mark was quoted in Tokyo late Wednesday at 71.38 yen. \par \par \uc2  Sterling is at $1.5235, down from $1.5237 earlier in Tokyo and unchanged from in New York late Wednesday. Sterling was at $1.5230 in Tokyo late Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Traders said the trend for the dollar probably was down over the next few sessions, weaking slowly but surely against European \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  But the combination of the BOJ's agressive \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  over the last month and tensions between China and Taiwan make it difficult to drive the dollar lower than the 105-yen level, traders said. \par \par \uc2  Market participants think the Deutsche Bundesbank won't cut interest rates at their policy meeting later Thursday. But given the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's tendency to do whatever isn't expected, no one rules out a surprise move. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 13-03-96 \par \par \uc2  0220GMT \par \par \uc2  1046 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011013ds3e029wn\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
