\par\par \b \uc2  World  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  -4: 105.00 Yen Support Seen Solid For Dlr \b0\par\par\uc2 298 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 1996\par 23:23\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1996, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile Tuesday, traders said the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's recent series of market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  - buying dollars and selling yen - seems to have established a dollar support level at 105.00 yen. \par \par \uc2  Tuesday, traders were reluctant to venture below that mark. The dollar only briefly touched its intraday low of 104.97 yen, at 1023 GMT. \par \par \uc2  However, the dollar isn't making any large gains against the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  either. Long-Term Credit's Pettit said there was substantial commercial interest Tuesday to buy dollars at 104.80 yen and sell dollars at 105.50 yen, holding the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in a tight range. \par \par \uc2  He said the yen is finding support from expected repatriation of Japanese capital before the March 31 fiscal year-end. \par \par \uc2  'I'm sure there have been some flows representing (yen repatriation) because of necessary year-end window dressing, but I don't see a huge amount of evidence of it,' he said. \par \par \uc2  While the market didn't seem to react Tuesday to news that China plans a week of surface-to-surface missile tests beginning Friday in waters off Taiwan, Pettit said, continued aggression so close to Japan could lead to some yen selling. \par \par \uc2  The move by China is widely seen as part of the country's campaign to intimidate Taiwan before the island's first direct presidential elections March 23. \par \par \uc2  The news pressured the New Taiwan dollar (NT) Tuesday, with dealers saying the Taiwan \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to keep the U.S. dollar below NT$27.50. At the close of Taiwan's official trading session at 0800 GMT, the U.S. dollar was quoted flat from Monday at NT$27.497. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 05-03-96 \par \par \uc2  2223GMT \par \par \uc2  1033 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011013ds3501yf5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
