\par\par \b \uc2  Japan spends $15 bln in Feb to keep yen down. \b0\par\par\uc2  By George Nishiyama \par \uc2 654 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 Februar 1996\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1996 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, Feb 29 (Reuter) - The Bank of Japan bought an estimated $15.3 billion for yen in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  in February, the largest amount on record, bankers said on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  The previous record for its monthly purchases was an estimated $14.07 billion in March 1995. In January, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is believed to have refrained from any \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The estimated record purchase is the result of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's aggressive \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , widely seen at preventing a revival of a strong yen, which would undermine prospects for Japan's fragile economic recovery, bankers said. \par \par \uc2  "The BOJ's (Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's) \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is not aimed at guiding the dollar higher to a specific level, but to prevent it from sliding, because a fall below 100 yen would undermine prospects for the country's economic recovery," said Ichiro Ikeda, vice-president at Goldman Sachs International Bank in Tokyo. \par \par \uc2  Data released by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Thursday showed that capital outlays from the government's special \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  account to the private sector totalled 2.007 trillion yen ($19.2 billion) in February. \par \par \uc2  The figure comprises yen payments from the government's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  account to the private sector, mainly commercial banks. \par \par \uc2  The payments are a result of the BOJ's dollar-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  for yen and the maturing of financing bills previously sold to the market by the Finance Ministry. \par \par \uc2  A total of 408 billion yen ($3.92 billion) was paid to the banking sector to cover the maturity of the financing bills. \par \par \uc2  The remaining 1.599 trillion yen ($15.3 billion) is seen as representing the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's dollar-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , bankers said. \par \par \uc2  The figures include the last two trading days of the previous month, but not the last two of this month, as \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  settlements are made two days after transactions. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's record buying also owes in part to help from its overseas counterparts, bankers said. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  amount covers apparent dollar purchases by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore on behalf of the Bank of Japan on February 23 and also dollar buying by the Bank of England on the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's behalf on February 27. \par \par \uc2  In a rare acknowledgment of such moves, Japanese Finance Minister Wataru Kubo said on February 23 that measures such as \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and cooperative action among major nations were being taken to prevent the dollar from falling. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the volume of dollar purchases by Singapore and the Bank of England for the BOJ in overseas markets was estimated to have reached well over $6 billion in those two days. \par \par \uc2  The apparent Singaporean support was the first such action carried out under a pact unveiled on February 20 allowing the Bank of Japan to ask its counterparts in Singapore and Hong Kong to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets on \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's behalf. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been under downward pressure as the recent rise in Japanese money market interest rates is believed to have triggered dollar sales from U.S. hedge funds. \par \par \uc2  U.S. hedge funds, which until recently borrowed low-cost yen and then invested the funds in higher-yielding instruments, including U.S. stocks and bonds, are widely believed to have begun to review their strategy. \par \par \uc2  Japan's fiscal year-end on March 31 was also believed to have been behind the Bank of Japan's buying, bankers said. \par \par \uc2  The dollar tends to sag ahead of the book closings at the year-end as Japanese firms repatriate or liquidate foreign assets to book profits or limit losses. \par \par \uc2  In spite of the heavy purchases, the dollar fell to this year's low of around 103.30 yen in New York trade on February 27. It regained some lost ground and stood at 104.55/60 yen in late Tokyo trade on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1996 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011019ds2t00t08\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
