\par\par \b \uc2  = \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  View: Dollar Seen Steady Against Yen Through March \b0\par\par\uc2  By David Mulholland \par \uc2 299 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 Februar 1996\par 22:38\par \uc2  Capital Markets Report \par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1996, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  NEW YORK (Dow Jones)--Market watchers expect Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to strive to keep the dollar strong until the end of Japan's fiscal year on March 31. \par \par \uc2  To prop up the dollar, the Bank of Japan bought around $5 billion to $6 billion last week, entering the market every day except Monday. \par \par \uc2  "The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  has to keep \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Kevin Harris, an international economist with MCM \b \highlight22\uc2 CurrencyWatch\b0 \highlight\uc2  in New York. He added that a weaker yen has been instrumental in preserving Japan's weak economic recovery. \par \par \uc2  If the yen strengthens, it could could hurt Japan's beleaguered banking system as the island nation's fiscal year draws to a close, analysts said. \par \par \uc2  The banking crisis in Japan has left many banks struggling to write off bad loans, said David Solin, a principal at \b \highlight22\uc2 Foreign Exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  Analytics in New York. The banks have to keep up their reserves. And if the dollar falls, the yen value of U.S. Treasurys and other foreign assets falls, which will hurt the already shaky banks, he said. \par \par \uc2  MCM's Harris pointed out Japan's central bankers have more at stake than just the economy: "If they don't succeed in keeping the yen about where it is, the bureaucrats would be blamed for it." \par \par \uc2  The Bank of Japan may allow the dollar to ease from its current level around 105 yen, but slowly, economists say. \par \par \uc2  "They might let it drift down to 102, 103 but slowly, letting the market know it won't be easy until the end of March," said Gary Sakamoto, vice president of Treasurys and marketing at National Australia Bank in New York. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) DOW JONES NEWS 02-25-96 \par \par \uc2  1638EST \par \par \uc2  4077 4137 4340 \par \par \uc2 Dokument cm00000020011013ds2p00hag\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
