\par\par \b \uc2  Asia  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  Roundup -2: Some Estimate BOJ Bought $6 Bln \b0\par\par\uc2 273 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 Februar 1996\par 07:32\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1996, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  Traders said Japanese importers bought the dollar on dips, but that the BOJ was the most enthusiastic buyer in the market. \par \par \uc2  Some traders estimate the BOJ has spent as much as $5.0-$6.0 billion in defending the dollar over the last week. Friday marked the fourth consecutive day the BOJ has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. \par \par \uc2  'They've had to absorb a lot of the hedge funds' selling,' one Tokyo city bank trader said. \par \par \uc2  Despite the negativity, some traders say the market is simply repositioning after the dollar was overbought, and that if U.S. financial markets prove themselves back on track, the dollar could be bought again Friday. \par \par \uc2  Japanese Finance Minister Wataru Kubo said Friday that the dollar remains in a long-term reversal trend, but traders said the dollar's months-long upturn may be over. \par \par \uc2  Kubo also said he expects \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  as well coordinated \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  with the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's counterparts in order to ensure the orderly reversal of the dollar's decline against the yen. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of England was seen buying the dollar for yen in European trading Thursday. \par \par \uc2  In the remainder of the global day Friday, traders said the market will be looking ahead to U.S. gross domestic product growth data at 1330 GMT, and to Germany's January M3 money supply data at an unspecified time. \par \par \uc2  But traders said they aren't expecting that data to have much of an impact on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 23-02-96 \par \par \uc2  0632GMT \par \par \uc2  1034 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011013ds2n01mju\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
