\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  players ready to call Bank of Japan's bluff. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Kaori Enjoji \par \uc2 664 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Februar 1996\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1996 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, Feb 22 (Reuter) - After three consecutive days of Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  (BOJ) \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the novelty factor is wearing off quickly and dealers say they are eager to test the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's resolve in putting a floor under dollar/yen. \par \par \uc2  The first round of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Tuesday boosted the dollar by nearly three yen, coupled with an announcement that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  had joined in an \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  pact with other Asian central banks. \par \par \uc2  But from the second day onwards, the dollar has opened weaker in Europe despite rounds of BOJ buying in Tokyo. \par \par \uc2  "I'm surprised the market hasn't tested their resolve as they have in the past," said Alex Jackson, assistant manager at Nikko Bank in London. "Despite the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  stability pact, there's a lot more power in the market out there so it's a dangerous game the BOJ is playing." \par \par \uc2  Key U.S. fund names have cropped up selling dollars above the 105.50 yen level, a painful reminder of the past for the BOJ, when dealers relished the chance to sell dollars at better levels after each round of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  A break of a key technical level at 104.80 may act as the catalyst for a dollar sell-off as early as this afternoon, with stop losses looming below 104.50, dealers said. It stood at 105.19/26 yen at 0925 GMT, down from 105.30/35 on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  "It's cat and mouse with the BOJ," said Larry Hatheway, senior \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  economist at UBS in London. "The game is going to go on for some time." \par \par \uc2  Not only do dealers savour the memory of failed BOJ \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the past, this time they are backed by a hunch that the Japanese authorities may have to give a higher priority to its own economy and not merely focus on the level of the yen. \par \par \uc2  "On its own the BOJ is fighting a losing battle especially since interest rates have started to rise. The trend for the dollar is still south with the BOJ creating an artificial barrier around 105 for the moment," said Kay Haigh, senior \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  economist at Deutsche Morgan Grenfell in London. \par \par \uc2  Last year, Japan's economy suffered a major setback as the yen powered to a post-World War Two high of around 79.70 yen. \par \par \uc2  "I think deep down the BOJ would like to tighten (credit). The question is which objective is more imporant -- setting an exchange rate floor or domestic considerations," Hatheway said. \par \par \uc2  "I think eventually domestic considerations will win out." \par \par \uc2  After Tuesday's \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  pact announcement, Japan has been trying various tactics to keep the dollar above 105 yen. \par \par \uc2  On Wednesday, it tried verbally. \par \par \uc2  "We will not tolerate a strong yen. Those who had sold dollars at recent lows have got their fingers burnt. Those who sell dollars will be disappointed," the BOJ told Reuters. \par \par \uc2  Today, it tried electronically. \par \par \uc2  There was talk in Tokyo that the BOJ channelled \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  through electronic broking services, where the level and amount of each deal struck on the computer appears on the screen. The method, although not new, spreads the word fast, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers agree that for dollar-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to be most effective, the market has to be caught short and by surprise. \par \par \uc2  "You can almost set your watch by the BOJ with this latest bout of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said David Coleman, economist at Canadian Imperial Bank of Commerce. "It's not the way to do it." \par \par \uc2  Analysts say authorities may revert to politically manoeuvring dollar/yen off lows, adding that the weekend summit meeting between President Bill Clinton and Japanese Prime Minister Ryutaro Hashimoto would be key. \par \par \uc2  "The BOJ may be prepared to continue to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  by itself, but without support from the Fed and the Bundesbank, the BOJ will be unable to turn the dollar tide," said Haigh. \par \par \uc2  -- London newsroom + 44 171 542 6721 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1996 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011019ds2m0186g\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
