\par\par \b \uc2  Dollar Mixed Late In Asia In Thin, Nervous Market \b0\par\par\uc2 316 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 Februar 1996\par 06:53\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1996, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TOKYO (Dow Jones)--The dollar was mixed in late Asian trading Wednesday compared with levels in New York late Tuesday, testing lower against the yen, but up versus the Deutsche mark. \par \par \uc2  Traders said the Asian market was nervous and thin, after several days of highly volatile trading, and after Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Traders said the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  definitely was not in the market Wednesday, but BOJ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  Tuesday 'sent a clear message that it doesn't want the dollar below 105.00 yen,' a trader at a Japanese city bank said. 'There is a sense in the market that it's a little dangerous to take the dollar down that far.' \par \par \uc2  Traders said the news that Republican Pat Buchanan pulled a narrow victory in the New Hampshire presidential primary had no impact on Asian trading. As reported, with three-quarters of the vote counted, Buchanan led the field with 27% of the vote, leading supposed front-runner Robert Dole's 26%. \par \par \uc2  'Conceivably (Buchanan's victory) is dollar-bearish news,' a trader at another Tokyo city bank said. 'He's a trade hawk, and he may favor a weaker dollar to help U.S. exports. But I don't think it had any impact (Wednesday).' \par \par \uc2  Around 0530 GMT, the dollar is quoted at 105.15 yen, below 105.69 yen late Tuesday in New York and down from 106.10 yen late Tuesday in London. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  also is at 1.4540 Deutsche marks, higher than 1.4475 marks late Tuesday in New York but up a little from 1.4535 marks in London Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  The mark is quoted at 72.31 yen, well down from 73.02 yen in New York late Tuesday and below 73.00 yen in London late Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 21-02-96 \par \par \uc2  0553GMT \par \par \uc2  28038 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011013ds2l01kg3\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
