\par\par \b \uc2  Japanese stocks in London drop as Dow, FTSE slip. \b0\par\par\uc2 369 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 Februar 1996\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1996 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, Feb 20 (Reuter) - Japanese shares in London traded mostly lower on Tuesday, unsettled by falls in New York and London stocks as bond markets plunged, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "When it became clear that New York was going to open quite weak on bonds, people started to kick prices down," said one trader. \par \par \uc2  The Nikkei/ISE 50 ended 4.40 points down at 1391.17. The Dow Jones index plunged more than 60 points in the first 20 minutes of trade, hit by falls in U.S. Treasuries and by investors' concern ahead of Federal Reserve Chairman Alan Greenspan's testimony. \par \par \uc2  London's FTSE 100 index fell to a low of 3702.7 after New York opened but managed to recover to stand 31 points down at 3713.3 by late afternoon trading. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said shares started the session in London with a positive tone, buoyed by a rebound in the dollar following \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the dollar and the announcement of an Asia \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  pact. \par \par \uc2  The dollar jumped more than two yen on rounds of dollar buying by the Bank of Japan starting at about 104.45 yen and up to the 106 level. \par \par \uc2  Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  also announced that Japan, Hong Kong and Signapore had reached an agreement allowing the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  to ask its Asian counterparts to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in dollar-yen trading on its behalf. \par \par \uc2  Among blue-chip stocks, Canon received an extra boost after Tokyo closed when the company announced its consolidated 1995 pre-tax profit soared 51.3 percent to 117,234 million yen. \par \par \uc2  By midday, traders said nervousness over a weak Dow open and losses on the FTSE-100 index started to weigh on shares. \par \par \uc2  "There wasn't a lot of trading going on, just people ticking down prices," said one trader. \par \par \uc2  Shares extended losses made in the domestic market, where the Nikkei 225 fell 65.58 points or 0.32 percent to 20,655.67 after losing more than 311 points earlier in the session on the dollar's plunge overnight. \par \par \uc2  -- Merissa Marr, London Newsroom +44 171 542 4027 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1996 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011019ds2k01e1w\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
