\par\par \b \uc2  Japan  \highlight22\uc2 currency \highlight\uc2  pact amounts to little - analysts. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Phil Smith \par \uc2 679 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 Februar 1996\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1996 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, Feb 20 (Reuter) - Hong Kong and Singapore's agreement to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's behalf is of limited significance and will only lend modest support to the dollar, financial analysts said on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  "There is little exceptional or substantive in this agreement," said Avinash Persaud, head of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  research at J.P. Morgan. \par \par \uc2  "The Asian central banks have not agreed to use their own reserves to support the Bank of Japan but merely to act on its behalf," he added. \par \par \uc2  He also noted that Japan already has similar agreements with a host of other central banks, including the Federal Reserve, but this did not stop dollar/yen falling below 100.00 last year. \par \par \uc2  But the announcement of the agreement -- coming as it did alongside aggressive BoJ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  -- did give the dollar a boost, pushing it up two and half pfennigs/yen to around 1.4600 marks and 106.50 yen. \par \par \uc2  "The timing of the announcement was impeccable. Not only was it a holiday but it was when the dollar had fallen to 103-yen and at a time when the market had the potential to move the most," said Jiro Nagato, senior dealer at Sumitomo Bank. \par \par \uc2  Even if the timing of the announcement was aimed at giving dollar/yen a bit of a boost, the Bank of Japan itself was pouring cold water on the idea that the pact was aimed to rein in the yen. \par \par \uc2  A BoJ spokesman said Japan started discussions with Singapore and Hong Kong last year and the decision about the timing of the announcement was made last week and was regardless of market conditions. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said the impact of the BoJ buying and the pact was probably greater than it otherwise would have been because it had got the market speculating about G7 dollar \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "Possibly one difference that BoJ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  through Singapore or Hong Kong will have from \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  through the Bundesbank or Fed is disclosure," said Steve Barrow, economist at Chemical Bank. \par \par \uc2  He said very often when the BoJ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  through a G7 \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  involved is keen to tell the market that it is acting on behalf of the BoJ. \par \par \uc2  "Whether this will be the case when the BoJ go through Singapore or Hong Kong remains to be seen," he said. "If they keep quiet it might keep the market guessing and possibly make the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  more effective." \par \par \uc2  There was certainly more talk of G7 \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the European market on Tuesday with traders speculating about the likelihood of a show of strength. \par \par \uc2  "They missed a golden opportunity late last week to get the dollar higher and now we are in a new lower trading range it will be more difficult to get it higher if they want to," said one trader. \par \par \uc2  "Maybe they will and maybe they won't. It's a tough one to call but people are ready for it and it's been the main topic of conversation in the dealing room this morning," she added. \par \par \uc2  Aside from possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the market will be closely watching Fed chairman Alan Greenspan's Humphrey-Hawkins testimony to congress. \par \par \uc2  His report on the current state of the U.S. economy is due to start at 1500 GMT and given the current confusion about growth his words will be carefully picked over. \par \par \uc2  "Greenspan cannot be too downbeat about growth prospects but he is sensitive to market concerns and may therefore seek to offer encouragement to easing hopes by again highlighting the real economy's current sluggishness," said Tim Fox, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  economist at Credit Suisse. \par \par \uc2  At 1140 GMT the dollar was 105.68/73 yen and 1.4510/15 marks, having drifted down gently from 106.08/17 and 1.4561/67 at the European opening. \par \par \uc2  It closed on Monday after a quiet session, with most of Asia and the U.S. on holiday, at 103.80/85 yen and 1.4428/38 marks. \par \par \uc2  -- London Newsroom, +44-71-542-6284. \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1996 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011019ds2k01dte\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
