\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  pact not aimed at halting strong yen-BOJ. \b0\par\par\uc2 312 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 Februar 1996\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1996 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, Feb 20 (Reuter) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's decision to ask other Asian monetary authorities to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on its behalf was not aimed as a measure to halt the strengthening of the yen, a senior Bank of Japan official told reporters on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  He said Japanese, Singaporean and Hong Kong authorities started discusssing the cooperative ties last year and decided last week to make the announcement at the beginning of this week regardless of market conditions. \par \par \uc2  He said that a recent shift towards a stronger yen was due to change in the market's view of interest rates. \par \par \uc2  Although the markets had expected interest rates to stay low for some time, recent moves, such as Germany's decision to keep its rates unchanged and Japan's announcement that its economic conditions were headed for a gradual recovery had changed sentiment. \par \par \uc2  He said there was a need to determine whether this shift in the markets reflected economic fundamentals. \par \par \uc2  He added that if this was the case, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would have to accept it. He said he wanted to hear Federal Reserve Chairman Alan Greenspan's comments to Congress later today to determine whether the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trend reflected fundamentals. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was also watching Germany's money supply data, to be released later this week. \par \par \uc2  The official said the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  pact, under which the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will ask Hong Kong and Singapore to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in dollar-yen trade on its behalf in their markets, was agreed upon in order to strengthen cooperative ties with Asian countries. \par \par \uc2  He explained that Singapore and Hong Kong markets tend to lead market sentiment, and asking other monetary authorities to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  for \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  will help in keeping secrecy. He added that another reason was that local traders know their markets best. \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1996 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011019ds2k01693\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
