\par\par \b \uc2  Dollar soars on Japan's dollar-yen announcement. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Miki Shimogori \par \uc2 568 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 Februar 1996\par 08:41\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1996 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, Feb 20 (Reuter) - The dollar jumped nearly three yen on Tuesday, buoyed by Tokyo's announcement of a pact allowing its \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to ask counterparts in Singapore and Hong Kong to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets on \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's behalf. \par \par \uc2  The dollar rose to above 106 yen after the announcement. Earlier, repeated dollar buying by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 , combined with news that the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  pact would soon be announced, had boosted the greenback to near 106 yen. \par \par \uc2  "The monetary authorities of Hong Kong and Singapore and Japan recently formed an arrangement in which Hong Kong and Singaporean authorities \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the dollar-yen in their markets on behalf of Japanese authorities," Japan's Finance Ministry said in a statement. \par \par \uc2  "A similar arrangement has already existed between Australia and Japan for some years. The authorities of Australia, Hong Kong, Singapore and Japan believe that these arrangements will contribute to exchange market stability and will continue to cooperate closely in the market," it said. \par \par \uc2  Tokyo share prices, heartened by the dollar's surge, rebounded from morning lows early in the afternoon session. \par \par \uc2  The key Nikkei stock average finished the day down 65.58 points, or 0.32 percent, at 20,655.67 after falling as low as 20,409.91. \par \par \uc2  Economists said the announcement of the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  pact showed Japanese authorities were determined to prevent the nation's fragile economic recovery from being derailed by a strong yen, as it was last year after the dollar dropped to a post-war low of 79.75 yen on April 19. \par \par \uc2  In August, the Finance Ministry announced deregulation measures aimed at boosting Japanese investment abroad and supporting the dollar, and followed up with a second such package earlier this month. \par \par \uc2  The dollar rose as high 107.58 yen on January 31 but has since faltered. It plunged as low as 103.58 yen on Monday in overseas markets, when trading was thin due to Asia's lunar new year break and a U.S. market holiday. \par \par \uc2  As if to drive home the desire of the Japanese authorities for a stronger dollar, senior Finance Ministry official Eisuke Sakakibara told a seminar that the shifting of production overseas by Japanese firms and rising purchases of imports by Japanese consumers would not stop even if the dollar were to rise to a level of 110-115 yen. \par \par \uc2  But despite the dollar's surge, some economists expressed doubts that the Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  agreement itself would have much more than a fleeting impact on the dollar-yen rate. \par \par \uc2  "The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  was already capable of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  on its own behalf, there was no particular limit on its ability to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Peter Morgan, senior economist at James Capel Pacific Ltd. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealers said courage might be needed to sell dollars short-term, but the medium-term outlook for the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  remained muddled. \par \par \uc2  "The dollar's downward risks have become smaller, although we need to keep a close watch on the U.S. stock and bond markets," said a senior dealer at a Japanese bank. \par \par \uc2  An official at Japan's Finance Ministry said the agreement with Hong Kong and Singapore was reached on February 16 in Kyoto, western Japan, at the same time as a meeting of deputy finance ministers from the Asia-Pacific Economic Cooperation (APEC) forum. \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1996 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011019ds2k0168u\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
