\par\par \b \uc2  Dollar outlook blue despite Asia  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  pact. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Yoshiko Mori \par \uc2 770 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 Februar 1996\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1996 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, Feb 20 (Reuter) - Although \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  showed its determination on Tuesday to check the dollar's slide with a surprise announcement of a tie-up with other Asian central banks, traders said the short-term outlook for the dollar was still bearish. \par \par \uc2  Japanese monetary authorities on Tuesday unveiled a pact allowing the Bank of Japan (BOJ) to ask its counterparts in Singapore and Hong Kong to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in dollar-yen trade on its behalf. \par \par \uc2  Aggressive dollar buying by the BOJ, combined with the announcement, pushed up the dollar to 106.60 yen in Tokyo. \par \par \uc2  Yukuo Takahashi, managing director of Chemical Bank's Tokyo branch, said: "The BOJ appears overconfident about the effect of its successful \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  last year, as it simply followed through on the market momentum for the natural upward correction of the dollar." \par \par \uc2  However, the short-term dollar trend is bearish as commercial dollar buyers have already bought as much as their demand warranted and the market is in an overbought position concerning the dollar, Takahashi said. \par \par \uc2  Furthermore, the slow pace of the U.S. economic recovery and lingering uncertainties about Europe's monetary union are encouraging the market to be long on the mark, he added. \par \par \uc2  Yasuhiko Matsunaga, senior manager at the Industrial Bank of Japan Ltd's International Treasury Department, said: "The pact does not provide any solution to the recent softness of the dollar, which is rooted in such factors as bearish U.S. Treasuries and Wall Street markets, which are nervous over the downside risk." \par \par \uc2  But he said the announcement created market sentiment in which speculative dollar sales below 105 yen were difficult. \par \par \uc2  Given the narrowing trend in Japan's external surplus, a safety pact such as the one announced today may well have a short-term impact on the market, Chemical's Takahashi said. \par \par \uc2  "The other aim of the pact is to indirectly check dollar selling by other Asian central banks by making clear the BOJ's intention to support the dollar," Matsunaga of IBJ said. \par \par \uc2  Takashi Okura, chief dealer of First National Bank of Chicago's Tokyo branch, said: "Repayments of the yen loans which Japan had made to other Asian economies depressed the dollar against the yen early last year. Today's move appears to be a first step toward checking such an action." \par \par \uc2  The next move will be to allow borrowers of the yen loans to repay them in dollars, he added. \par \par \uc2  In early Tokyo trade there was a rumour, later denied by a Finance Ministry official, that Japan would make an announcement on allowing borrowers of government yen loans to pay back the debt in dollars. \par \par \uc2  Toyomitsu Sakata, head of Treasury sales at National Westminster Bank in Tokyo, said: "Asian nations borrowing yen loans could benefit from the yen's falls by lessening the burden of their repayments, but not all Asian nations will be happy to see a steep dollar rise." \par \par \uc2  The dollar's rapid rise against Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  has also put inflationary pressure on their economies by raising import prices, economists said. \par \par \uc2  Eisuke Sakakibara, director-general of the Finance Ministry's international finance bureau, told reporters that the pact was aimed at enhancing \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  stability. \par \par \uc2  "Since the yen's moves are not a major concern for European nations, which are preoccupied with a goal for a single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , or the Euro, Sakakibara might decide to team up with neighbouring Asian nations," Sakata added. \par \par \uc2  Asked if the agreement will influence Japan's stance towards so-called Asian "repo pacts", aimed at protecting Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  from speculative attacks, a senior Finance Ministry official said: "Although we have a great interest in any regional cooperation in the field of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , we cannot comment on a specific pact." \par \par \uc2  In November, \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and monetary authorities from Australia, Hong Kong, Indonesia, Malaysia and Thailand agreed to coordinate in stabilising Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  by supplying liquidity to each other using U.S. Treasury bonds as collateral. Japan has been wary of joining the repo pact. \par \par \uc2  In the Asia-Pacific region, the BOJ has occasionally bought dollars directly through banks in Singapore and Sydney, or checked dollar/yen rates as a step preceding \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The BOJ has also had a limited number of banks here discreetly buy dollars through U.S. and European banks in Singapore, traders said. \par \par \uc2  The tactic, which is in addition to ordinary dollar-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the Tokyo market, is seen aimed at the banks in Singapore which apparently handle the orders of overseas hedge funds, a major driving force in the foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, traders said. \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1996 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011019ds2k01689\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
