\par\par \b \uc2  Dollar soars on news of Japan  \highlight22\uc2 forex \highlight\uc2  announcement. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Miki Shimogori \par \uc2 570 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 Februar 1996\par 06:06\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1996 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, Feb 20 (Reuter) - The dollar, after suffering a heavy sell-off overnight, rebounded dramatically in Tokyo on Tuesday on the surprise news \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  will unveil plans to improve ways to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in overseas \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets later in the day. \par \par \uc2  Repeated dollar buying by the Bank of Japan also fuelled an aggressive dollar-buying spree, traders said. \par \par \uc2  The greenback soared to nearly two yen to 106 yen by Tokyo midday after senior Finance Ministry officials said the ministry would soon make an announcement concerning \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  with overseas monetary authorities such as those in Singapore and Hong Kong. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile Tokyo share prices, heartened by the dollar's surge, rebounded from their morning lows in early afternoon on Tuesday. The key Nikkei stock average was at about 20,640 in early afternoon trade after closing at 20,470.20 at midday. \par \par \uc2  A government source said \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  will announce an \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  scheme in which it will be able to ask Asian monetary authorities to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on behalf of the Bank of Japan (BOJ). \par \par \uc2  The ministry and the BOJ said they will hold separate announcements on Tuesday afternoon. \par \par \uc2  Economists said the announcement suggested Japanese monetary authorities were strongly determined to support the dollar. \par \par \uc2  "I got a feeling that there is a really strong will in the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the Bank of Japan to push the dollar towards 110 yen," Makoto Kojima, director of Global Markets at Barclays Bank, told Reuters Financial Television (RFTV). \par \par \uc2  Their determination was also backed up by action, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  appeared to have \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  at least twice in Tokyo morning trade, initially buying dollars at above 104.45 yen then at around 105.30 yen just before Tokyo midday, Tokyo bankers said. \par \par \uc2  The move added fresh jitters to the market, prompting buying back of the dollar, which fell as low as 103.58 yen on Monday in overseas markets, where trade was dampened by Asia's lunar new year holidays and a U.S. market holiday. \par \par \uc2  With Japanese authorities showing strong determination to stem the yen's rally, traders may need courage to sell dollars in the near-term, but the medium-term outlook is still muddled. \par \par \uc2  "The dollar's downward risks have become smaller, although we need to keep a close watch on the U.S. stock and bond markets," said a senior dealer at a Japanese bank. \par \par \uc2  Earlier, the dollar temporarily came off its highs against the yen as a Finance Ministry official denied rumours Japan planned to announce measures on Tuesday to allow borrowers of government yen loans to pay the debt back in dollars. \par \par \uc2  Despite the apparent BOJ buying, Finance Minister Wataru Kubo said on Tuesday morning that the level of the dollar, which was at around 104 yen at the time of his comment, was not a major worry. \par \par \uc2  Kubo also told a news conference that his ministry had no immediate plans to announce new deregulation measures. "I have nothing especially to say here at the moment, but deregulation is the main political and administrative target." \par \par \uc2  Earlier this month, the Finance Ministry said it would ease restrictions on foreign investments and \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  transactions to promote overseas investment by Japanese, a move which \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealers said was aimed at giving the dollar a boost. \par \par \uc2  The package followed other steps announced last August. \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1996 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011019ds2k01606\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
