\par\par \b \uc2  Japan  \highlight22\uc2 forex \highlight\uc2  plan shows will to help dlr - economists. \b0\par\par\uc2 347 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 Februar 1996\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1996 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, Feb 20 (Reuter) - Japanese financial authorities' planned announcement of a new \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  scheme with Asian monetary authorities shows their determination to support the dollar for the sake of Japan's fragile economy, economists said on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  "I got a feeling that there is a really strong will in the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the Bank of Japan to push the dollar towards 110 yen," Makoto Kojima, director of global markets at Barclays Bank, told Reuters Financial Television (RFTV). \par \par \uc2  Ron Bevaqua, an economist at Merrill Lynch Japan Inc, told RFTV that the move showed Japan's concern for its economy. \par \par \uc2  Bevaqua said that although the dollar's plunge against the yen overnight was simply a temporary correction in the long- trend of a weakening yen, it was enough of a threat to make the BOJ and MOF think they had to do something to make sure the yen remained on a more consistent and obvious weaker trend. \par \par \uc2  "I think that suggests that they are still concerned about the state of the economy. They don't want any threats to it from the dollar-yen rates," Bevaqua said. \par \par \uc2  He added that the market had reacted "seriously and positively" to the planned scheme, as shown in the dollar's jump of more than two yen by Tokyo midday. \par \par \uc2  Bevaqua said the scheme had been in the works and that the authorities had been waiting for the right time to announce it. \par \par \uc2  "They probably do have a list of options available to them should the yen start to strengthen again," he said. \par \par \uc2  Kojima said the dollar should "go up definitely" as the day progresses, and Bevaqua predicted a possible rise to above 106 yen by the end of the day. \par \par \uc2  The MOF and BOJ said they would make an announcement at 2.30 p.m. (0530 GMT) on a new \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  scheme in which \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  would be able to ask Asian monetary authorities to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on the behalf of the BOJ. \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1996 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011019ds2k015zl\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
