\par\par \b \uc2  Yen Falls On BOJ  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Reports, Pact: World  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2  By REBECCA H. PATTERSON \par \uc2 294 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 Februar 1996\par 22:38\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1996, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  NEW YORK (AP-Dow Jones)--The yen weakened Tuesday against most major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  on reports the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2 , buying dollars for yen, and on a Japanese government announcement of plans to enlist other countries' help with \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Although the Japanese news bolstered the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Asian dealings Tuesday, the dollar lost steam in Europe, leveling off around 106.00 yen for the remainder of the global trading day. \par \par \uc2  The dollar also rose against the Deutsche mark Tuesday, again rising in the Asian session only to slip in later trading. \par \par \uc2  The dollar began climbing against the yen and mark Tuesday on reports that the Bank of Japan had entered \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets to buy dollars for yen. \par \par \uc2  Tokyo dealers estimated the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  spent between $700 million and $1.0 billion for the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which was said to have continued throughout the Asian day. \par \par \uc2  The yen further weakened after Japanese Finance Ministry announced arrangements to let Hong Kong and Singapore monetary authorities \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  on behalf of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  in dollar-yen trading in their respective markets. \par \par \uc2  At the end of the global trading in New York, the dollar was quoted at 105.69 yen, up from 103.95 yen in London Monday. The last time the dollar was lower against the yen than Monday's late London level was Jan. 3, when it hit 103.88 yen. There was no New York trading Monday due to a holiday. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was also quoted at 1.4475 marks, up from 1.4450 marks late Monday in London. Sterling was at $1.5457, down slightly from $1.5460. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 20-02-96 \par \par \uc2  2138GMT \par \par \uc2  1033 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011013ds2k01jq2\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
