\par\par \b \uc2  Early Tokyo: Dlr Up; Market Waits For Signs Of BOJ Action \b0\par\par\uc2 313 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 Februar 1996\par 01:35\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1996, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TOKYO (AP-Dow Jones)--The dollar is higher in early Tokyo trading Tuesday than its levels late in London Monday, in choppy trading as the market waits for presumed \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  'If the BOJ doesn't come in (Tuesday) morning, the dollar is going to drop sharply,' said the head of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading at an American bank in Tokyo. \par \par \uc2  Swift action by Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is seen by many as necessary to prop up the dollar after it fell Monday in the wake of the sharp drop by the South African rand last week, and general disappointment over the dollar's inability to maintain its gains. \par \par \uc2  Around 0030 GMT, the dollar is trading at 104.45 yen, up from 104.15 yen around 0001 GMT and above 103.95 yen in London late Monday. The dollar was quoted at 105.13 yen late in Tokyo Monday. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is also trading at 1.4480 Deutsche marks, higher than 1.4465 marks around 0001 GMT and above 1.4450 marks late Monday in London. The dollar was at 1.4500 marks in Tokyo late Monday. \par \par \uc2  The mark is trading at 72.13 yen, up from 72.00 yen around 0001 GMT and above 71.94 yen in London late Monday. The mark was quoted late in Tokyo Monday at 72.50 yen. \par \par \uc2  Sterling is at $1.5480, down from $1.5484 around 0001 GMT but above $1.5460 in London late Monday. Sterling was at $1.5460 in Tokyo late Monday. \par \par \uc2  Describing the market as 'volatile,' a trader at a Japanese bank said that while 