\par\par \b \uc2  Japan Stocks -3:  \highlight22\uc2 Currency \highlight\uc2  Market Holds Key For Wednes. \b0\par\par\uc2 280 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 Februar 1996\par 08:18\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1996, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  The Nikkei ranged between 20,409.91 and 20,668.03 during the course of the day's trading. Its intraday low was its lowest point since Jan. 26, but its late rally allowed it to close near its intraday high and above recent technical support at its 25-day moving average. That average was around 20,653 Tuesday and should be slightly lower Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Within the context of a broad range of 20,000-21,000, the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market and the stance of overseas investors hold the key to share price movements in the coming days, players say. \par \par \uc2  There were hopeful signs of buying from domestic financial institutions - particularly banks - when the Nikkei fell below 20,500, players said. Selling from those institutions has quashed several market rallies in recent months. \par \par \uc2  But nobody was making any hard predictions given the rapid swings in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. \par \par \uc2  If the dollar moves back down below 105.00 yen, weakness in New York might carry over into the Tokyo share market Wednesday, said Tim Reed, head of equity trading at BT Securities Asia. 'If the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  is still at the current level, we might be ready to rally a bit,' Reed added. \par \par \uc2  Since the announcement by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the Bank of Japan of agreements with the monetary authorities of Hong Kong and Singapore to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  on behalf of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  in dollar-yen trading in their markets, the dollar had risen to 106.20 at 0715 GMT, down from a high of 106.60 yen just after the stock market closed. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 20-02-96 \par \par \uc2  0718GMT \par \par \uc2  5011 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011013ds2k01h0g\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
