\par\par \b \uc2  Asia  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  Roundup-2: Dollar Seen To Reach 107.50 Yen \b0\par\par\uc2 327 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 Februar 1996\par 07:31\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1996, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  At 0530 GMT, Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  and Bank of Japan announced that they reached agreements with monetary authorities of Hong Kong and Singapore arranging for those authorities to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  on behalf of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  in dollar-yen trading in their markets. They noted that a similar arrangement already existed with Australia for some years. \par \par \uc2  The announcement pushed the dollar still further to a peak at 106.60 yen around 0604 GMT, traders said. \par \par \uc2  Moreover, traders say there were rumors of further dollar-buying by the BOJ at 106.05 yen to coincide with the announcement, which rallied U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  buying by interbank players in particular. \par \par \uc2  The chief \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer at a major Japanese commercial bank said the market started taking profits by selling dollars at the low-106.00-yen level prior to the press conference, from wariness about the content of the finance ministry's announcement. He said, however, that as the content was 'as expected' by the market, participants started to buy back the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  He said the bullish momentum of the dollar is likely to be carried on to European and U.S. markets, leading the dollar up to 107.50 yen in global dealings Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Should the dollar break through 107.50 yen Tuesday, he said, further gains up to 108 yen are possible this week. \par \par \uc2  Rumors that Eisuke Sakakibara, director of the Japanese finance ministry's international finance bureau, would announce Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  cooperation in \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  filtered through the market from 0240 GMT, following traders' reports that the BOJ bought dollars at 104.50 yen around 0115 GMT and again at 105.20 yen around 0230 GMT. The dollar fell to the high-103.00-yen level on Monday. \par \par \uc2  There were also rumors that the BOJ bought dollars above 106.00 yen around 0445 GMT. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 20-02-96 \par \par \uc2  0631GMT \par \par \uc2  1034 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011013ds2k01gty\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
