\par\par \b \uc2  Early Tokyo: Dlr Mixed As 106.00 Yen Level Seen Important \b0\par\par\uc2 326 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Februar 1996\par 01:39\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1996, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TOKYO (AP-Dow Jones)--The dollar is mixed in early Tokyo trading Thursday from its levels late in New York Wednesday, with traders wary that Japan's government may take measures to prevent it from going below 106.00 yen. \par \par \uc2  Around 0030 GMT, the dollar is trading at 106.23 yen, down from 106.27 yen around 0001 GMT and below 106.29 yen in New York late Wednesday. The dollar was quoted at 106.73 yen late in Tokyo Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is also trading at 1.4650 Deutsche marks, higher than 1.4646 marks around 0001 GMT and above 1.4643 marks late Wednesday in New York. The dollar was at 1.4695 marks in Tokyo late Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  The mark is trading at 72.51 yen, down from 72.56 yen around 0001 GMT and below 72.59 yen in New York late Wednesday. The mark was quoted late in Tokyo Wednesday at 72.63 yen. \par \par \uc2  'The 106.00 level is very sensitive,' said a dealer at an American bank in Tokyo. 'If the dollar continues to dip below that, Japan's monetary authorities may make public more details of market deregulation measures.' \par \par \uc2  Last week, when the dollar fell to the 104.80-yen level, Japan's government announced a series of proposals to make overseas investment easier for trust banks and insurance companies. That pushed the dollar up sharply, to 107.40 yen, before it resumed its current decline. \par \par \uc2  The American bank dealer said that as details of the proposals were sketchy, the government could release further details to prop up the dollar. \par \par \uc2  A Japanese dealer at another American bank in Tokyo even argued that the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  could \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to push the dollar up, saying that the rumors last week of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  should be taken seriously. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 14-02-96 \par \par \uc2  0039GMT \par \par \uc2  1046 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011013ds2f01dot\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
