\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Japan \highlight\uc2  to boost funds for  \highlight22\uc2 forex intervention \highlight\uc2  - MOF. \b0\par\par\uc2 163 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 Dezember 1995\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1995 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, Dec 29 (Reuter) - The Japanese government is likely to boost the ceiling on its financial resources for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market in the budget for fiscal 1996/97, a \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  spokesman said on Friday. \par \par \uc2  The government is likely to raise the ceiling on financial bills (FBs) by six trillion yen in the next fiscal year from 33 trillion yen in the current fiscal year ending March 31. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  (MOF) raises cash for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by issuing FBs. An increase in the FBs will mean the MOF will have the ability to step up \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market next year if necessary, dealers said. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought a hefty amount dollars for yen in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets to halt the yen's sharp rise earlier this year. \par \par \uc2  The MOF official declined to comment on how much of its financial bills quota the ministry had used this year. \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1995 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011103drct009fm\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
