\par\par \b \uc2  Japan Govt/Dollar -4: Growth In Eastern Europe Noted \b0\par\par\uc2 265 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Dezember 1995\par 01:51\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1995, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  The report also noted the existence of continued growth in Eastern Europe as well as signs of recovery in Russia. \par \par \uc2  Continued rapid growth in Asia and a slowdown in Oceania were also mentioned in the report as significant developments during 1995. \par \par \uc2  Concerning trends in international financial markets the report focused on the dollar's sharp decline against both the yen and Deutsche mark during the first half of the year and its subsequent recovery that began in July. \par \par \uc2  In April, the dollar hit its lowest level against the yen since the introduction of the modern exchange rate system in the late 1940s, dipping just below 80 yen. That same month Group of Seven (G-7) finance ministers and \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governors called for an 'orderly reversal' in the dollar's fortunes. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  (BOJ) maintained an aggressive stance, \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on an almost daily basis, buying dollars in an attempt to stem the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's slide. Several rounds of joint dollar-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the BOJ and other central banks reinforced the market view that the G-7 meant business. \par \par \uc2  The EPA noted, however, that many Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  actually increased their value against the dollar during its decline, a phenomenon the report said was different from past reactions to phases of dollar weakness. \par \par \uc2  The report said that dur